  "worked_solution": "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14099625/assets/3f071c27bfa281abcaabe63d4d67797ea7b051b931ee7658d2a32a58f80a0bac.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-xy, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R\u2216D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthen we obtain\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{D}({x}^{3}-xy)\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangle II does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangles I and III cover the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
